{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0HA2", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-G-scheme}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0dbbe665517adc8f4b7abd3c2f92d07cc2cac590b4b278f549f718fb5a0ae0ac", "source_text": "G-schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a85186b51fe0e42949f848d27b6ce11de8f89c49107313d9dbb3afd6fa2ee331", "unit_id": "tag:0HA2:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0HA2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathfrak p$", "MATH_0004": "$R$", "MATH_0005": "$R_\\mathfrak p \\to (R_\\mathfrak p)^\\wedge$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3edf0b34b62a29481a015859501ce3293962d12ec543405c2ab65c103d209923", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:179dc770178a52d6d8af6bebd75e518cc9b2526e5b79465a7a60995f46200f06", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe remark that a ring <MATH_0001> is a G-ring if <MATH_0002> is Noetherian and\nfor every prime ideal <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004> the ring map\n<MATH_0005> is regular.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be91b60946c8b99a07c23ad8b7d29636ba73ebbccea69bae14a3513d29847c1b", "unit_id": "tag:0HA2:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0HA2", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$G$", "MATH_0004": "$G$", "MATH_0005": "$G$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0007": "$x \\in U \\subset X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-G-ring}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-G-scheme}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:506ca2d021acf035be1bfc252ea16c8bd72cfbfb449dc4080f6657aa0be24cf8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4d776ef1c941280b90c460bd6e2e55448875866f953f006fb20327ab27ee8942", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. We say <MATH_0002> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>G-scheme<TEXTITCLOSE_0001><FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>This may be\nnonstandard terminology. If <MATH_0003> is a finite group or group scheme\nthen sometimes a <MATH_0004>-scheme denotes a scheme equipped with an\naction of <MATH_0005>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001> if for every <MATH_0006> there exists an affine\nopen neighbourhood <MATH_0007> such that the ring\n<MATH_0008> is a G-ring (see\nMore on Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:553e932604f3aa523811c3364e9509f1aee698ecd9ae20b923a7a2ac68a757cd", "unit_id": "tag:0HA3:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0HA2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}^\\wedge$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}^\\wedge$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-G-scheme}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:597b50dbbd0feb0f561187716b76dec7fcf0b8869ba142129c1cf1cf59afdf24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2f0eb9f88764d0337ab8dd1d3cc4a2d1eb659c0cd5e5af8c46d39d61ab676ef4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is a G-scheme,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is locally Noetherian and for all <MATH_0004> the ring\nmap <MATH_0005> is regular, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0006> is locally Noetherian and for any closed point <MATH_0007>\nthe ring map <MATH_0008> is regular.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:add5e85b8754af9fc4843a0a60d3fdf2d7e15f2ce6241dc8a3cc541c9f6bed7e", "unit_id": "tag:0HA4:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0HA2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\leadsto x'$", "MATH_0003": "$x'$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x'}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x'}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}^\\wedge$", "MATH_0009": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-Noetherian-closed-point}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-check-G-ring-maximal-ideals}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-specialize-points}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-locally-Noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5a6fdbeab9c592d16571a946ce2a17fadf3cfea2af7267f2f4c66eb481e9b649", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ed748acf6b591e43aab619d79ed0e685fd66d158dfa8a5cd86462c63147df96e", "source_text": "It is clear that (1) implies (2) and (2) implies (3).\nAssume (3). Let <MATH_0001> be any point. By\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthere exists a specialization <MATH_0002> with <MATH_0003> closed\nin <MATH_0004>. Then <MATH_0005> is a G-ring by\nMore on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nSince <MATH_0006> is the localization of <MATH_0007>\nat a prime ideal (Schemes, Lemma <REF_0003>),\nwe see that <MATH_0008>\nis a regular ring map. Since <MATH_0009> was arbitrary we conclude\nthat for any affine open <MATH_0010> the Noetherian\n(Lemma <REF_0004>) ring <MATH_0011> is a G-ring.\nThis proves that (1) holds.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11259dddbb02b4821868198ca134c24324e07ca783f091fb736dc819039f6cdc", "unit_id": "tag:0HA4:proof"}
